new file mode 100644
index 00000000..b34d993e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+# CVE-2021-22570 — False Positive Assessment for protobuf-java 3.5.1
+
+## Summary
+
+**CVE-2021-22570 does not affect `com.google.protobuf:protobuf-java` 3.5.1.**
+The defect is in the C++ `protoc` compiler (`DescriptorBuilder` in
+`src/google/protobuf/descriptor.cc`), not in the Java runtime JAR. There is
+nothing to patch in this artifact.
+
+---
+
+## CVE Description
+
+> Nullptr dereference when a null char is present in a proto symbol. The
+> symbol is parsed incorrectly, leading to an unchecked call into the proto
+> file's name during generation of the resulting error message. Since the
+> symbol is incorrectly parsed, the file is nullptr. We recommend upgrading
+> to version 3.15.0 or greater.
+
+- **CVE ID:** CVE-2021-22570
+- **GHSA:** GHSA-77rm-9x9h-xj3g (withdrawn 2025-08-25)
+- **Severity:** originally High (CWE-476 NULL Pointer Dereference)
+- **Upstream fix commit:** `51daaba638941cdd04c0ed349a70d3742c42de4d`
+- **Fix released:** Protocol Buffers 3.15.0
+- **NVD:** https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-22570
+
+---
+
+## Scanned Package
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Ecosystem | Maven |
+| Package | `com.google.protobuf:protobuf-java` |
+| Version | `3.5.1` |
+| Artifact | Java runtime (`java/core`) |
+| Scanner mapping | Often listed as affected if `< 3.15.0` |
+
+---
+
+## Root Cause of the CVE
+
+The crash is in **protoc**, while it formats a parse-error message for a
+symbol, package, or file name that contains a NUL byte (`\0`).
+
+`DescriptorBuilder` incorrectly treats the NUL-truncated name as valid enough
+to look up the owning file, then dereferences a null `FileDescriptor` when
+building the error string. That code lives only in the C++ compiler:
+
+```
+src/google/protobuf/descriptor.cc
+```
+
+Official fix commit `51daaba638941cdd04c0ed349a70d3742c42de4d` changes that
+C++ file only. It does not touch `java/core` or any file published inside
+`protobuf-java-3.5.1-sources.jar`.
+
+The 3.15.0 release note for this fix is also C++-only:
+
+> Ensure that null char symbol, package and file names do not result in a crash.
+
+---
+
+## Why protobuf-java 3.5.1 Is Not Affected
+
+### 1. Upstream: compiler bug, not a runtime bug
+
+The Protocol Buffers maintainers confirmed this in
+[protocolbuffers/protobuf#9483](https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/issues/9483):
+
+> This issue was with the protoc compiler itself not any of the runtimes.
+
+`protobuf-java` is the Java runtime. It does not embed `protoc` and does not
+link `descriptor.cc`.
+
+### 2. The official fix commit has no Java hunks
+
+`51daaba` only edits C++ compiler sources. A Java 3.5.1 sources JAR has no
+those files, so there is no equivalent change to apply.
+
+### 3. GitHub / GitLab Maven advisories were withdrawn
+
+[GHSA-77rm-9x9h-xj3g](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-77rm-9x9h-xj3g)
+was withdrawn on **2025-08-25**:
+
+> This advisory has been withdrawn because the protobuf vulnerability comes
+> from the compiler rather than the code.
+
+GitLab's Maven advisory for `com.google.protobuf:protobuf-java` repeats the
+same withdrawal text.
+
+### 4. Why scanners still flag 3.5.1
+
+NVD and older GHSA ranges listed `protobuf-java < 3.15.0` because the
+protobuf version number is shared across language artifacts. That mapping is
+incorrect for the Java runtime. A finding against
+`com.google.protobuf:protobuf-java:3.5.1` should be suppressed.
+
+The real affected component is an old **`protoc` binary** (before 3.15.0),
+used at codegen time — not this Maven JAR at runtime.
+
+---
+
+## Conclusion
+
+**CVE-2021-22570 is a false positive for `com.google.protobuf:protobuf-java:3.5.1`.**
+
+| VEX | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Status | `not_affected` |
+| Justification | `vulnerable_code_not_present` |
+
+No Java source change is required. If a scanner flags this CVE on 3.5.1,
+suppress it. Fix the compiler by using `protoc` ≥ 3.15.0 when generating
+code from `.proto` files.
+
+---
+
+## References
+
+- Official compiler fix: https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/commit/51daaba638941cdd04c0ed349a70d3742c42de4d
+- Upstream confirmation: https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/issues/9483
+- Withdrawn GHSA: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-77rm-9x9h-xj3g
+- NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-22570
+- v3.15.0 notes: https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/releases/tag/v3.15.0

